{
 "section_summary": "Pages 1–36 contain a Strategic Services Unit report on the January 1946 election of Japanese residents’ representatives in Shanghai, including election rules, candidate statements, results and press commentary. The remaining pages concern investigations into the wartime conduct and loyalty of Franklyn Gustav Lewis, a former American consular clerk interned in Mukden. They include an FBI forwarding letter, intelligence memoranda and corrections to an earlier report.",
